.Dd July 30, 2026
.Dt LIBNOTIFYCMP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm notifycmp_client_open ,
.Nm notifycmp_subscribe ,
.Nm notifycmp_unsubscribe ,
.Nm notifycmp_publish ,
.Nm notifycmp_next ,
.Nm notifycmp_timer_add ,
.Nm notifycmp_timer_cancel ,
.Nm notifycmp_stats ,
.Nm notifycmp_client_close
.Nd bounded capability-component notifications
.Sh LIBRARY
.Li libnotifycmp
.Pq Fl lnotifycmp
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In notifycmp.h
.Ft int
.Fn notifycmp_client_open "struct notifycmp_client **client"
.Ft int
.Fn notifycmp_subscribe "struct notifycmp_client *client" "const char *topic"
.Ft int
.Fn notifycmp_publish "struct notifycmp_client *client" "const char *topic" "const void *payload" "size_t length"
.Ft ssize_t
.Fn notifycmp_next "struct notifycmp_client *client" "struct notifycmp_event *event" "size_t capacity" "uint32_t timeout_ms"
.Ft int
.Fn notifycmp_timer_add "struct notifycmp_client *client" "uint64_t timer_id" "uint32_t interval_ms" "uint32_t flags"
.Ft int
.Fn notifycmp_timer_cancel "struct notifycmp_client *client" "uint64_t timer_id"
.Ft int
.Fn notifycmp_stats "struct notifycmp_client *client" "struct notifycmp_stats *stats"
.Ft void
.Fn notifycmp_client_close "struct notifycmp_client *client"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library connects to the global
.Dq org.5bsd.notify
service through
.Xr libservice 3 .
It provides exact-topic publish and subscribe, bounded payloads and queues,
and owner-scoped one-shot or periodic monotonic timers.
applications do not supply component or provider names.
.Pp
.Fn notifycmp_next
dequeues one event.
A timeout of zero polls, while
.Dv NOTIFYCMP_TIMEOUT_INFINITE
waits without a deadline.
Each open creates an independent provider session, receive queue, request
sequence, and exchange lock.
Threads sharing one client are serialized so replies cannot cross, while a
blocking
.Fn notifycmp_next
on one client does not stall another client.
An inherited client is invalid after
.Xr fork 2 ;
the child must open a fresh session.
.Pp
Topics are dot-separated identifiers.
Empty segments, path syntax, control characters, and embedded NUL bytes are
rejected.
Published payloads are opaque bytes and publisher identity is supplied by the
trusted router.
Each session is deny-by-default until the provider has an authenticated,
identity-bound exact-topic publish and subscribe policy and a separate timer
grant.
The trusted publisher field remains part of application-level authorization;
topic permission alone does not authenticate message contents.
.Pp
A successful
.Fn notifycmp_publish
reply means that the router evaluated the publication and attempted fanout.
It is not a durable-delivery acknowledgement.
Subscriber queues are volatile and bounded; a full queue drops the newest
event for that subscriber and records the loss in statistics.
Events are not replayed after subscriber or router restart.
Callers needing durable delivery require a separate typed queue protocol with
stable event identifiers, consumer offsets, acknowledgements, and
deduplication.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kqueue 2 ,
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr capsicum 4 ,
.Xr notifycmp 8
